<header><p class="st-kicker">princely state · Indian princely states</p><h1 class="st-title">Kanker State</h1><p class="st-meta">1385 CE – 1948 CE (approx.) · capital Kanker</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">A small Gond-country princely state in the hills of present-day Chhattisgarh, ruled from Kanker until 1948.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>Kanker has inscriptions of local Somavanshi rulers from the 12th and 13th centuries; tradition dates the later ruling family to 1385. Its early history is only partly known.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>Kanker was a forested state with a mainly <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gond-people">Gond</a> population. In the 18th century it came under the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bhonsles">Bhonsles</a> of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/nagpur-kingdom">Nagpur Kingdom</a>, passing under British control in 1853 and becoming one of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chhattisgarh-feudatory-states">Chhattisgarh Feudatory States</a>.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>Kanker merged into the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/central-provinces">Central Provinces</a>, later <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/madhya-pradesh">Madhya Pradesh</a>, in 1948 and is now a district of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chhattisgarh">Chhattisgarh</a>.</p><p class="st-conf">Few sources survive for this state; details are uncertain.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/kanker-state.jpg" alt="Kanker State" width="320" height="202"><figcaption>Image: QuadrangleDinglePingle · CC0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_Kanker_(Princely_State).png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1385 CE – 1948 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/14th-century">14th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>princely state</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>feudal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Kanker</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Hinduism</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Chhattisgarhi, Gondi</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/india">India</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Kanker</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1666&amp;focus=kanker-state" aria-label="Kanker State on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="6876 1427 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Kanker State lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M7196 1683L7126 1652M7196 1683L7364 1602M7196 1683L7018 1386"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M7126 1652h0M7364 1602h0M7018 1386h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M7196 1683h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M7196 1683h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks its recorded location. <a href="/atlas?year=1666&amp;focus=kanker-state">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
